<description>
Recolor the right-side target column-runs with the left palette colors in order.

Input structure
- The background surrounds full-height, single-color palette columns on the left
  and a single-color target drawing on the right.
- Each target column has one contiguous vertical span, and adjacent columns with
  the same span form one rectangular run.
Rule
- Remove the palette and target marker color, leaving the background elsewhere.
- Read the palette columns from left to right.
- Recolor the target column-runs from left to right with the corresponding
  palette colors.
Key insight
- The target drawing is not a connected-component problem: its visible blocks are
  the maximal adjacent column groups that share the same vertical extent.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_in_order",
  "src": "full-height palette columns s on the left, ordered left to right",
  "dst": "maximal target-color column-runs d on the right: adjacent columns sharing one contiguous vertical span, ordered left to right",
  "match_cond": "rank(s) == rank(d)",
  "transform": "replace each d's target color with the corresponding s.color; all other cells become background"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 6-8 rows x 15-28 cols; bg=black(0)
  palette:
    count: 3-6 full-height single-color columns on the left
    position: columns 1,3,5,... (start at col 1, every other col; col 0 is bg)
    colors: distinct non-bg non-8 colors; order matters (left-to-right)
    gaps_between: always 1 bg column between adjacent palette columns [observed]
  target:
    color: always azure(8)
    location: all target columns strictly right of all palette columns
    gap_from_palette: 1-2 bg columns between rightmost palette and leftmost target col
    structure: N rectangular column-runs (N = palette count), each run is a contiguous horizontal group of columns sharing the same vertical span
    run_width: 2-4 columns per run
    run_height: 2-5 rows per run (each run can differ)
    run_gap: 0-1 bg columns between consecutive runs
    each column within a run has one contiguous vertical fill (no holes)
  output:
    same grid size; palette columns and target color removed (all bg)
    each target run recolored with corresponding palette color (left-to-right matching)
generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick N in [3,6], grid height H in [6,8]
    2. Choose N distinct colors from 1-9 excluding 8 for the palette
    3. Generate N rectangular runs for the output, each with width in [2,4] and height in [2,5], arranged left-to-right with gap 0-1 between runs; vertical positions vary freely within [0, H-1]
    4. Compute target area width = sum of run widths + sum of run gaps; palette area width = 2*N (palette at cols 1,3,...,2N-1); gap_to_target = randint(1,2)
    5. Grid width = 2*N + gap_to_target + target_area_width + padding (0-1 trailing bg cols)
    6. Build input: place palette columns at cols 1,3,...,2N-1 (full-height, each a single palette color); place all runs as color 8 in the target area; fill rest with bg
    7. Build output: place each run recolored with corresponding palette color; fill rest with bg
